    <briefdescription>
<para>Test cases are named sequences of checks. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Each test case is defined by calling <computeroutput>suite::test()</computeroutput> with a descriptive name and a callable object (typically a lambda accepting a <computeroutput>test_case&amp;</computeroutput> reference), along with any optional arguments required for the test. The test case runs immediately, within the call. Nested test cases are defined with <computeroutput>test_case::test()</computeroutput>, and a test case for each value of a range or a tuple with <computeroutput>test_each()</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>Test cases allow related checks to be organised together within the same environment, improving clarity and maintainability. Any number of test cases may be defined, each focusing on a specific aspect of the code under test.</para>
<para>By grouping checks in this way, developers can identify which functionality is being verified and interpret results in the context of overall software quality.</para>
